ot\models A_{ ot}(c). By applying this argument repeatedly, we would be able to build a model in which no individual satisfies A⊥A_{ ot}, which we have already proven to be impossible. It follows that there exists some b∈𝖭𝖨b\in\mathsf{N_{I}} s.t. for all models ℐ\mathcal{I} of 𝒯′,𝒜′\mathcal{T}^{\prime},\mathcal{A}^{\prime}, we have ℐ⊧A⊥​(b)\mathcal{I}\models A_{ ot}(b).
